{"book":"factors","bookTitle":"Multiples, factors and prime numbers","concept":7,"title":"Highest common factor (HCF)","grades":"Grade 7","goal":"I can find the highest common factor of two or three numbers.","teach":"The <b>HCF</b> is the biggest number that divides exactly into each of the numbers. List the factors and find the biggest one in every list. Or use prime factors: multiply the primes the numbers <b>share</b>.","tvis":"<div class=\"vis\"><span class=\"vi\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:494px;height:auto\" viewBox=\"0 0 380 192\"><circle cx=\"147.1\" cy=\"96.0\" r=\"78.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" fill-opacity=\"0.55\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><circle cx=\"232.9\" cy=\"96.0\" r=\"78.0\" fill=\"#fff\" fill-opacity=\"0.35\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"100.3\" y=\"16.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">60</text><text x=\"279.7\" y=\"16.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">84</text><text x=\"108.1\" y=\"101.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">5</text><text x=\"190.0\" y=\"81.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">2</text><text x=\"190.0\" y=\"101.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">2</text><text x=\"190.0\" y=\"121.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">3</text><text x=\"271.9\" y=\"101.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">7</text></svg></span><div class=\"cap\">Prime factors of 60 and of 84. They share 2, 2 and 3, so the HCF is 2 × 2 × 3 = 12.</div></div>","ex":{"q":"Find the HCF of 24 and 36.","steps":["Factors of 24: 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 12, 24.","Factors of 36: 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 9, 12, 18, 36.","The biggest factor in both lists is 12."]},"watch":"The HCF can never be bigger than the smallest of the numbers.","qs":[{"text":"Find the HCF of 16 and 40.","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"HCF","a":"8","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"Factors of 16: 1, 2, 4, 8, 16.","steps":"1. Rule: the HCF (highest common factor) is the biggest number that divides into all the numbers. List the factors and pick the biggest shared one, or multiply the shared prime factors.<br>2. Factors of 16: 1, 2, 4, 8, 16<br>3. Factors of 40: 1, 2, 4, 5, 8, 10, 20, 40<br>4. HCF = 8"},{"text":"Find the HCF of 45 and 75.","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"HCF","a":"15","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"Write both numbers as products of primes.","steps":"1. Rule: the HCF (highest common factor) is the biggest number that divides into all the numbers. List the factors and pick the biggest shared one, or multiply the shared prime factors.<br>2. 45 = 3 × 3 × 5; 75 = 3 × 5 × 5<br>3. Shared primes: 3 and 5<br>4. HCF = 3 × 5 = 15"},{"text":"The Venn diagram shows the prime factors of 90 and 126. Find their HCF.","vis":"<div class=\"vis\"><span class=\"vi\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:494px;height:auto\" viewBox=\"0 0 380 192\"><circle cx=\"147.1\" cy=\"96.0\" r=\"78.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" fill-opacity=\"0.55\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><circle cx=\"232.9\" cy=\"96.0\" r=\"78.0\" fill=\"#fff\" fill-opacity=\"0.35\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"100.3\" y=\"16.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">90</text><text x=\"279.7\" y=\"16.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">126</text><text x=\"108.1\" y=\"101.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">5</text><text x=\"190.0\" y=\"81.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">2</text><text x=\"190.0\" y=\"101.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">3</text><text x=\"190.0\" y=\"121.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">3</text><text x=\"271.9\" y=\"101.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">7</text></svg></span></div>","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"HCF","a":"18","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"Multiply the shared primes.","steps":"1. Rule: the HCF (highest common factor) is the biggest number that divides into all the numbers. List the factors and pick the biggest shared one, or multiply the shared prime factors.<br>2. 90 = 2 × 3 × 3 × 5; 126 = 2 × 3 × 3 × 7<br>3. Shared primes: 2, 3, 3<br>4. HCF = 2 × 3 × 3 = 18"}]}